From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:19:56 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: Return zero for an unconfigured PLL0822x
 divider

An unconfigured PLL can report a zero pre-divider. Avoid dividing by
zero when recalculating its rate and report an unavailable clock instead.
The existing Tensor G4 bring-up source carries this guard, while the
0516x/0517x/0518x PLL types themselves already exist in the public base.
This does not program PLLs or establish power-management support.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c
index e74552846..853a7343f 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-pll.c
@@ -461,6 +461,9 @@ static unsigned long samsung_pll0822x_recalc_rate(struct clk_hw *hw,
 	pdiv = (pll_con3 >> PLL0822X_PDIV_SHIFT) & PLL0822X_PDIV_MASK;
 	sdiv = (pll_con3 >> PLL0822X_SDIV_SHIFT) & PLL0822X_SDIV_MASK;
 
+	if (!pdiv)
+		return 0;
+
 	fvco *= mdiv;
 	if (pll->type == pll_0516x)
 		fvco *= 2;
